(Stage 1e3 review — `nothing` through a `value` RETURN and a `value` local.
 Test 188 covers a value parameter carrying nothing; the return path is a
 different route (tag 6 loaded into r11 by emit_load_value_tag's static arm,
 read back by the caller), and reading the result must dispatch on that tag
 rather than on the call's static type.)

To "echo" with a value called "v". Return a value, v.

print "echo" of nothing.
If "echo" of nothing is nothing, print "return round-trip ok".
Otherwise print "return round-trip LOST".

a value called "slot" is "echo" of nothing.
print slot.
If slot is nothing, print "local ok".
Otherwise print "local LOST".

set slot to 5.
If slot is nothing, print "retag LOST".
Otherwise print "retag ok".

a list called "L" is [].
append "echo" of nothing to L.
append 0 to L.
print L.
